WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:01.934
Every ticket names an asset,

2
00:00:01.934 --> 00:00:06.112
so the help desk can only be as
right as the inventory behind it.

3
00:00:06.112 --> 00:00:11.262
The book's position is clear: the CMDB
is a projection, not the authority.

4
00:00:11.262 --> 00:00:16.304
Discovery and connectors fill it, but
identity comes from the naming plane,

5
00:00:16.304 --> 00:00:19.150
the IP address management and DNS records.

6
00:00:19.150 --> 00:00:22.003
ServiceNow's engine
already decides whether a

7
00:00:22.003 --> 00:00:25.075
record is new and which
source may write each field.

8
00:00:25.075 --> 00:00:29.572
The book adds one more pass: match
each asset to the naming plane,

9
00:00:29.572 --> 00:00:33.550
bind that identity, and flag
anything that doesn't match.

10
00:00:33.550 --> 00:00:35.496
A shadow asset is a finding,

11
00:00:35.496 --> 00:00:39.475
and a gap gets fixed upstream,
never patched in the CMDB.

12
00:00:39.475 --> 00:00:41.660
Then come the everyday defects.
